phase P9
title Hardening and budgets
description
    **Class:** verifiable.

    **Kind:** performance.

    **Goal:** the budgets met on their named devices, and every finding from every round given a
    disposition.

    **Starts when:** P8's completion audit passes and the user has set the targets.

    **Verified by:**

    - P8's benchmark and real-browser suites;
    - skill:check-benchmark on baseline and final numbers;
    - a test-harness-only review by an agent with no prior reading;
    - the final review.

    **One iteration:** one finding group or one budget: one isolated change, measured against the
    accepted baseline, kept only if the checked comparison shows a gain with the tests green.

    **Exit criteria:**

    - budgets met on their devices;
    - every finding has a disposition;
    - quota and disk durability measured on a real phone by the user;
    - `nub run verify` and the final-commit gates pass.

    **False pass:** closing findings as dropped to finish.

    **Caught by:** the completion audit checking each drop's reason against the Specs.

    **Gates:** P8's slowed builds; falsify.

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:** the real-phone run, which holds only that item; a guarantee change.

    **User's read:** each finding's disposition.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:playbook-performance;
    - skill:hillclimb;
    - skill:check-benchmark.
tasks
    T36
        title       Budgets met on named devices
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        description
            Meet each budget on its named device, one budget at a time against P8's baseline.

            **Why now:** the budgets are the P9 goal; P8's baselines and the user's targets are what they are measured
            against.

            **Read first:** @task.V3.T35, skill:playbook-performance, skill:hillclimb, skill:check-benchmark.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a speedup that skips work → caught by skill:check-benchmark.
            - **Gates:** P8's slowed builds.
        acceptance
            Every budget met on its device in a checked comparison.
    T37
        title       Every finding given a disposition
        status      draft
        priority    medium
        description
            Sweep every finding from every round, Epic note and revisit.md into fixed, deferred with a reason, or
            dropped
            with a reason checked against the Specs.

            **Why now:** the P9 exit needs every finding to have a disposition before the final-commit gates.

            **Read first:** code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/revisit.md,
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/open-items.md, code:workflow/tasks/V3/epic.task.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** drops to finish → caught by the completion audit.
            - **Gates:** `nub run verify`.
            - **User's read:** each disposition.
        acceptance
            Every finding has a disposition; the final-commit gates pass.
    T38
        title       Quota and disk durability on a real phone
        status      draft
        priority    low
        description
            Prepare the real-phone script for quota and disk durability, and read the results the user runs.

            **Why now:** an agent here reaches only browsers and a simulator, and a WebDriver session keeps no website
            data, so quota and durability were never measured on a real store.

            **Read first:** code:packages/flow-state-v3/prototypes/safari/RESULTS.md (item 0 and the open quota and
            durability items), @task.V3.T36.

            - **Evidence:** this Task's comments.
            - **False pass:** a simulator standing in for the phone → caught by the user's own run.
            - **Stops:** the user's run.
            - **User's read:** the results.
        acceptance
            The user's real-phone results are recorded and meet the budgets.
